 "inference": [
  "EA's 'missile acceleration' is EngineStrength: the MBT-LAW stores 100, EA's new value.",
  "Max speed follows the registry-over-own pattern again: Glaive own 60, registry 70 (EA 60 to 70); helicopter TOW own 90, registry 120 (EA 90 to 120). The MBT-LAW has no row and its own value is 300, EA's new value.",
  "The IGLA missile file stores max speed 640 and engine strength 65, EA's values from before 1.3.1.0, and has no registry row; no SLM-93A file stores 480 either (400, 350 and 540). EA's 480 m/s for both is not in any file read here.",
  "Lock time is in the weapon file: IGLA 1.0 and Glaive 1.4, EA's new values. SLM-93A stores 1.5 and the MBT-LAW 3.0, for which EA states nothing.",
  "Each locking weapon file stores two lock ranges. The lower SLM-93A range is 550, EA's new base range. The higher is 1.2 times the lower for the IGLA (700, 840) and Glaive (650, 780), which fits EA's 'consistent 20% increase' from the laser designator; for the SLM-93A it is 1.25 times (550, 687.5), which does not.",
  "Active protection: Field_85c11a9b is 0.55, EA's 1.3.3.0 activation time. The same object stores 32, equal to the registry RechargeTime, and 4.0 where the registry ActiveTime is 5.0."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "IGLA and SLM-93A missile speed (stored 640 and 400 / 350 / 540; EA 480). Test: time an IGLA missile over a known distance to a hovering helicopter at about 480 m; 1 s after launch speed-up means 480 m/s.",
  "SLM-93A designated lock range: 687.5 m stored, 660 m by EA's 20 percent. Test: lock a laser-designated helicopter at 675 m.",
  "Which SLM-93A missile file the gadget fires (PB_NS_Stinger or PB_Stinger); the weapon-to-projectile import was not traced here.",
  "Active protection active time: own 4.0 or registry 5.0. Test: time the system's active window."
 ],
